Modifications
=============

`silo/dashboard.json` is a modified version of `dashboard.json`, as permitted
by section 4 (b) of the Apache License, Version 2.0. The changes are:

1. Panels removed.

   The original had 37 panels; this version keeps 13. The following original
   panels were removed, grouped by the feature they covered:

   - KMS (5 panels): KMS Uptime, KMS Request 4xx Error Rate,
     KMS Online(1)/Offline(0), KMS Request 5xx Error Rate and
     KMS Request Success Rate. The target deployment has no KMS.
   - Erasure set and healing: Health Breakdown and Time Since Last Heal.
   - Scanner counters: Scanned Objects, Scanned Versions,
     Scanned Directories, Bucket Scans Started and Bucket Scans Finished.
     "Time Since Last Scan" was not removed but repurposed, see item 5.
   - Internode traffic: Internode Traffic. The target deployment is
     single node.
   - Process internals not needed for a single node deployment: Goroutines,
     Open FDs, File Descriptors, Syscalls, Read/Write I/O, Memory Usage and
     CPU Usage. Memory Usage and CPU Usage were folded into one new
     "Process (CPU / RSS)" panel.
   - Cluster and node counters that are constant on a single node cluster:
     Cluster Health Status, Total Online Servers, Total Online/Offline
     Drives, Total S3 Ingress, Total S3 Egress, S3 API Ingress Rate and
     S3 API Egress Rate. The last two were merged into one new
     "Network traffic" panel.
   - Object size distribution: Object Size Distribution.
   - Multi node capacity pie chart: Capacity. It was replaced by a new
     "Capacity (usable)" time series panel.

   The panels that were kept keep the visual template of the original panel
   they were built from (panel type, field configuration and options). Only
   the title, the description, the queries, the legends and the layout were
   changed.

2. Template variables added.

   A `host` variable (`label_values({__name__=~"minio_.*"}, host)`) was added
   and every query now filters on `host=~"$host"`. The `scrape_jobs` variable
   was constrained to the Silo scrape job
   (`label_values(minio_cluster_usage_objects_total_bytes, job)`) instead of
   listing every job in the cluster, and every query filters on
   `job=~"$scrape_jobs"`. The original aggregated across every scraped job
   (bare `sum(...)` / `max(...)`, or `by (server)` / `by (instance)`); this
   version groups by `host` (`sum by (host)` / `max by (host)`) because the
   cluster level series carry a `host` label but no `server` label and are
   emitted by every node, so a bare sum would count the same bytes twice.

3. Per bucket usage fixed.

   The original "Data Usage Growth" panel queried
   `max(minio_cluster_usage_buckets_total_bytes)`, which reports only the
   largest bucket. This version uses `sum by (host, bucket)` for the new
   "Usage per bucket" table and `sum by (host)` for the "Data used" headline.

4. `or vector(0)` added to rate expressions.

   Silo v3 only exports values greater than zero, so a silent but healthy
   node would blank a panel. Every rate expression is now wrapped in
   `or vector(0)`. The two drive panels pair the drive metric with
   `minio_system_drive_total_bytes` using
   `or on(host, drive) (0 * ...)`, so a drive that stops reporting is held at
   0 (0 bytes free, offline) instead of disappearing from the panel.

5. Scanner metric repointed.

   "Time Since Last Scan" pointed at `minio_usage_last_activity_nano_seconds`,
   a metrics v2 name that Silo v3 no longer exports. It now reads
   `minio_scanner_last_activity_seconds`, which reports seconds rather than
   nanoseconds, and the "Uptime & scanner lag" panel also shows
   `minio_cluster_usage_objects_since_last_update_seconds` to caption the age
   of the usage metrics.

6. Renamed to remove MinIO branding.

   The dashboard title is "Silo — Object Storage", the uid is
   `silo-object-storage` and the tags are `silo` and `storage`. Panel titles,
   legends, descriptions and colour overrides were reworded accordingly, and
   the links to other MinIO dashboards were removed.

7. Data source changed.

   The dashboard reads the `victoriametrics` data source instead of the
   default `prometheus` one, because the Silo metrics are only present in a
   central VictoriaMetrics store in the target deployment.

8. Layout re-flowed, one panel type added.

   The grid positions were re-flowed for the 13 panels. The original
   dashboard had no table panel, so the new "Usage per bucket" panel is a
   table built for this fork.
